## The Change

In [`libs/migrate/src/migrate/legacy_source.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/src/migrate/legacy_source.py#L463-L476), the SQLite tick reader arm built `obj` from only the columns present in the SQLite schema (`t_dict.items()`). When evaluating pre-chain SQLite stores (era-1) where `since` or `(prev_hash, window_start, fact_cursor, window_hash)` columns do not exist on the table, `row_object_fault` rejected the row for missing fields before checking `TICK_NULLABLE`.

We updated the tick arm object builder to construct the row object over all canonical `TICK_FIELDS`:
```python
obj = {f: t_dict.get(f) for f in TICK_FIELDS}
if t_dict.get("signature") is not None:
    obj["signature"] = t_dict["signature"]
```
Absent SQLite columns evaluate to `None`, which `TICK_NULLABLE` (`frozenset(("since", *TICK_CHAIN_FIELDS))`) explicitly permits.

Alongside, added [`build_era1_sqlite`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/tests/_fixtures.py#L687-L728) in `_fixtures.py` and test coverage in [`test_inventory.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/tests/test_inventory.py#L320-L334) and [`test_transform.py`](file:///Users/kaygee/Code/loops-wt/s4-wp2/libs/migrate/tests/test_transform.py#L576-L633).

